// Caricatures of each city's real water, drawn loosely around its circuit (world/water.js places them).
// Frame: the circuit's bounding box is [-1,1] on both axes; x runs east, y runs south. The game may turn a sketch
// by quarter turns to fit its circuit, and pushes any water that comes too near the road back out, so shapes only
// need to be roughly right. Widths (w) are world units (the road is 8.6 wide).
//   {band:[[x,y],...], w}            a river or channel along a smooth path
//   {arc:[cx,cy,r,deg0,deg1], w}     a band along a circular arc (0 deg = east, 90 = south)
//   {poly:[[x,y],...]}               a closed body of water (bay, lake, harbour basin)
//   {hug:'N'|'S'|'E'|'W'[, w]}       sea on that side, its shore following the circuit (or a channel w wide)
//   land:true                        drawn as land over the water (islands, piers, the Palm)
//   straight:true                    (on a poly) keep its long edges straight; only the corners round off
//   drift:[dx,dy]                    which way the glints on it drift
//   {landmark:[x,y], heading:[dx,dy]} pins the city's landmark to this spot, its long side along heading (e.g. the
//                                    opera house along Bennelong Point)
//     pad:[length,width]              ...on a patch of land that size (world units), so it never overhangs the water
//   {bridge:[[x,y],[x,y]]}           pins where the city's freeway bridge crosses (bank to bank)
//   {prop:{kind,color}, at:[x,y], heading:[dx,dy]} an extra landmark model at this spot (e.g. Hong Kong's wheel)
//   {focus:[[x,y],...]}              the full-track camera always shows these points (a lake the city is known by)
//   {road:[[x,y],...]}               a freeway along this path, traced from the real city (replaces the generated ones)
//     join:true                      ...whose first point is on an earlier road: a junction there, not a ramp or fade
//   {reclaim:m}                      the circuit always sits on land: land fills m units round it wherever water would reach
//   {turn:k}                         always place the sketch at this quarter turn (when other scenery depends on it)
//   {uniform:true}                   scale the sketch evenly on both axes (by the circuit's shorter side) rather than
//                                    stretching it to the circuit, for shorelines whose proportions matter
